---
import Breadcrumbs from '@/components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { breadcrumbs } from '@/lib/seo';
import { site } from '@/lib/site';

const crumbs = [
  { name: 'Home', href: '/' },
  { name: 'About', href: '/about/' },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Cuisdev"
  description="Cuisdev builds free developer tools that run entirely in your browser. Learn why we built it, how it stays private, and what is coming next."
  jsonLd={[breadcrumbs(crumbs)]}
>
  <div class="stack stack--lg">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
    <article class="prose">
      <h1>About {site.name}</h1>
      <p class="prose--lead">
        Cuisdev is a collection of small, fast developer utilities that run entirely in your
        browser. No accounts, no uploads, no ads chasing you around the page.
      </p>

      <h2>Why we built it</h2>
      <p>
        Every developer has pasted a JSON blob, a JWT or a Base64 string into some random website to
        inspect it. Most of those sites are slow, buried in ads, and quietly send your data to a
        server you know nothing about. That is a strange thing to accept for data that is often
        sensitive.
      </p>
      <p>
        Cuisdev exists to be the tool site you can recommend without a caveat: quick to load,
        pleasant to use, and incapable of leaking your data because it never leaves your machine.
      </p>

      <h2>How privacy works here</h2>
      <p>
        Every page is static HTML. The tools are small TypeScript programs that run in your browser
        using standard Web APIs. There is no backend that receives your input, so there is nothing
        to log, store or breach. You can load a tool, disconnect from the internet, and keep
        working.
      </p>
      <p>
        We do not use tracking cookies or third-party advertising scripts. See the
        <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for the details.
      </p>

      <h2>What is next</h2>
      <p>
        We are rebuilding Cuisdev from the ground up and shipping tools in clusters: JSON and data
        conversion, encoding and decoding, generators, text utilities, web and code helpers, and
        image tools. New tools are added regularly. If there is a utility you wish existed, tell us
        at
        <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
